# A proc call has no value, so it cannot be bound by `:=`. A statement-position
# `nop()` stays legal -- only a decl that would take `void` as its type is
# rejected. Same guard covers `ys := [nop()]` and `t := (1, nop())`, whose
# composed types carry a `void` component.
fn nop():
    print("x")

fn main():
    x := nop()
    println("unreachable")
